lay\" command every time a phone associates with the Bluetooth and the audio system was left \"on\".      reply                             kowbell    2 hours ago       |  root  |  parent  |  next   [–]       \n  I also have a 2014 CR-V and I hate this too. But even moreso, I hate that there isn't a play/pause button at all. If I need to stop audio (e.g. pulling up to a drivethru, or starting a conversation), I gotta hit the phone. Heaven forbid I'm playing a CD, nothing I can do at that point. Putting up a bug bounty of \"ordering you a pizza\" if anyone tackles this!      reply                             jandrese    1 hour ago       |  root  |  parent  |  next   [–]       \n  Had a Chevy that was extremely obnoxious about this.  If it was playing over USB it absolutely would not allow it to stop.  Hitting pause on the phone would have the car immediately hit play to restart it.      reply                             EvanAnderson    2 hours ago       |  root  |  parent  |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  I get pause (for Bluetooth playback, at least) by pushing the volume encoder knob. That works well for me.      reply                             rockostrich    4 hours ago       |  parent  |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  It's probably easier to just buy an aftermarket head unit. The only thing you'll need to confirm is that it supports features you care about e.g. steering wheel controls.      reply                             rithdmc    3 hours ago       |  parent  |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  Probably more difficult than hijacking the display with the pi. But that's just a vibe.      reply                             vessenes    3 hours ago       |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  Okay, this was gratifying to read, but ... can't you wedge CarPlay onto this thing? I'd want a victory lap with root doing at least something. Bad apple on car boot, there's lots of options here!      reply                             xx_ns    3 hours ago       |  parent  |  next   [–]       \n  Yeah, I'll keep working on this to get it to do more stuff that's at least a little bit more useful, if not just a better UI that isn't 90% a useless \"No maps found\" screen. It's more complicated than it might initially seem because they actually have a kernel module blocking me from mounting non-signed partitions as exec, so I'll need to work around that. I'll probably post a follow up if I get anywhere with this!      reply                             whycome    4 hours ago       |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  Pretty awesome write up to explain their journey in it all. I suspect a bunch of car head units will face new problems in the spring when many Canadian provinces will no longer change their clocks. The units won't get updated DST rules.      reply                             Niksko    2 hours ago       |  parent  |  next   [–]       \n  Happened to my Mazda the other day. Thankfully it supports just setting the timezone and dst flag manually.      reply                             monegator    3 hours ago       |  parent  |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  which is mind boggling. my skoda simply has an entry in the menu: DST? which puts the clock one hour ahead or behind. This posts remind me that when i will be in the market for a new van i will have to decide to get the trafic or the vivaro, solely on the head unit they use (renault ones have had incredibly stupid design decisions for years, on ergonomics alone, even more in firmware)      reply                             settsu    2 hours ago       |  root  |  parent  |  next   [–]       \n  Yep, in my mind this is one of the hallmarks of a well-designed digital desk clock: a 2-position hardware switch for DST on/off.      reply                             Groxx    1 hour ago       |  root  |  parent  |  next   [–]       \n  Well. In most places.  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daylight_saving_time#Procedure  (edit to be clear: not all places use 1 hour offsets)      reply                             settsu    1 hour ago       |  root  |  parent  |  next   [–]       \n  I lived for several years in a place that did not observe DST. At least that portion of living there was pretty nice.      reply                             iclelland    3 hours ago       |  parent  |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  That's this fall - happened a couple of days ago.      reply                             maelito    2 hours ago       |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  I wonder how many systems have a good web browser embedded. Last time it was tried on a tesla, it could barely render a maplibre map. The Web is a universal platform very capable in 2026.      reply                             yowayb    3 hours ago       |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  not quite as difficult, but reminds me of a fix I found on reddit for Subaru Outback parasitic drain:  https://www.reddit.com/r/subaru/comments/1evozzf/dead_batter...       reply                             1970-01-01    2 hours ago       |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  Usually you can just get a modern OBDII scanner and set it via the diagnostics or hot functions.      reply                             geephroh    3 hours ago       |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  Love it! Slightly more elegant than my solution: a piece of electrical tape over the clock.      reply                             speedgoose    3 hours ago       |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  The Renault Latitude is actually Samsung car right?      reply                             encom    2 hours ago       |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  I wish someone would jailbreak the Nissan Leaf (MY2018) head unit. Every time I turn on the car, it shows a EULA asking if Nissan can please collect every detail of my car at all times and sell it to whoever asks.  Every. Time.  Even if I beat my head with hammers to think like a lawyer, I can't imagine how it would be necessary to ask constantly. Doesn't matter if I accept or decline, it still asks again.      reply         