  "text": " \n \n\n     [2611.03596] Spacetime Emergence in the Memory of a Learning Agent \n   \n   \n   \n   \n   \n   \n   \n   \n   \n   \n   \n \n    \n    \n    \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n          \n   \n   \n   \n           \n \n\n  \n     Skip to main content \n  \n \n \n \n    \n   \n     \n   \n   \n     \n     Search \n   \n   \n     \n   \n   \n     Submit \n     Donate \n      \n Log in    \n \n \n   \n     \n       Search arXiv \n       \n       \n       \n     \n     \n      Press Enter to search &middot;  Advanced search \n     \n   \n \n\n     \n       \n \n     \n     \n--> \n\n   \n     \n       Quantum Physics \n     \n\n     \n       arXiv:2611.03596  (quant-ph)\n     \n \n \n   \n     \n  [Submitted on 2 Nov 2026] \n      Title: Spacetime Emergence in the Memory of a Learning Agent \n      Authors:  Philip A. LeMaitre ,  T. Rick Perche               View a PDF of the paper titled Spacetime Emergence in the Memory of a Learning Agent, by Philip A. LeMaitre and 1 other authors \n     View PDF \n     HTML (experimental) \n\n\n\n     \n             Abstract: We show that the causal structure of spacetime can emerge within the memory of a learning agent performing a quantum information task. We train a model-based reinforcement-learning agent to maximize the quantum mutual information between localized quantum probes interacting with a quantum field in Minkowski spacetime, without directly providing it with information regarding the spacetime metric or causal structure. In learning to accomplish this task, the reinforcement-learning agent constructs an internal predictive model whose planner develops the characteristic null structure of spacetime, allowing us to reconstruct the causal structure of the Minkowski metric with high accuracy. Within this task, spacetime geometry is obtained from an agent's successful predictions and actions, providing a first step toward showing that spacetime concepts emerge from operational quantum experience.\n     \n\n     \n     \n                \n           Comments: \n           19 pages, 7 figures \n         \n \n           Subjects: \n           \n             Quantum Physics (quant-ph) ; Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI); Machine Learning (cs.LG); General Relativity and Quantum Cosmology (gr-qc) \n          \n           Cite as: \n             arXiv:2611.03596  [quant-ph]  \n         \n         \n             \n           (or  \n               arXiv:2611.03596v1  [quant-ph]  for this version)\n           \n         \n         \n             \n                          https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2611.03596  \n               \n                 \n                 Focus to learn more \n               \n               \n               \n                                    arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite (pending registration) \n             \n           \n          \n     \n   \n \n     \n       Submission history  From: Philip Adam LeMaitre [ view email ]            [v1] \n        Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:39:52 UTC (3,134 KB) \n \n   \n   \n      \n        \n       Full-text links: \n       Access Paper: \n       \n   \nView a PDF of the paper titled Spacetime Emergence in the Memory of a Learning Agent, by Philip A. LeMaitre and 1 other authors   View PDF    HTML (experimental)    TeX Source\n    \n        \n           \n           view license \n          \n     \n          \n     Current browse context: \n   quant-ph \n\n   \n \n       < prev \n     \n       |        \n       next > \n      \n    \n     new \n      |  \n     recent \n      |   2026-11 \n    \n    Change to browse by:\n     \n         cs  \n         cs.AI  \n         cs.LG  \n         gr-qc  \n     \n   \n\n     \n       \n         References & Citations \n         \n             \n               INSPIRE HEP  \n             \n            SciX    Google Scholar  \n            Semantic Scholar  \n         \n          \n       \n\n \n     export BibTeX citation \n     Loading... \n \n\n \n     