ostman's ongoing enshittification...      reply                             ebtebt    1 hour ago       |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  Thank you for the reminder, I had not deleted Postman yet. Done :D      reply                             languagehacker    2 hours ago       |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  I've always kind of thought that Postman was an enshittification story waiting to happen. I've always felt like they prey on people who just aren't comfortable with the command line, and so there isn't much more stooping lower for them than something like this.      reply                             orphereus    2 hours ago       |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  Does everything have to go to shit when money is involved?      reply                             pizzafeelsright    2 hours ago       |  parent  |  next   [–]       \n  No. Postman sells nothing of value. At this point I do not see why the entirety of their software could not be a one shot prompt for the price of deer nuts.      reply                             paulddraper    1 hour ago       |  root  |  parent  |  next   [–]       \n  > price of deer nuts Which, in case others didn't know, are under a buck.      reply                             rs999gti    1 hour ago       |  parent  |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  Depends. Is it an investment grant or loan? The former is money to grow with no expectations on growth. The latter has an investor giving money in expectation of a return. Most of the YC companies are loan backed with investors pushing milestones for the next investment chunk or round.      reply                             autoexec    2 hours ago       |  parent  |  prev  |  next   [–]       \n  Pretty much. It's just a question of how fast it happens. The more capable something is of making money without compromising the product or exploiting users the longer it will take, but once people who are sick with pathological greed get involved they'll eventually start to demand enshittifying