 "page:https://www.gitbook.com/status/security-incident-2026-11-03": {
  "v": 3,
  "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T20:11:46.798Z",
  "bytes": 13605,
  "text": " \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\t \r\n\t \r\n\t \r\n\t Security incident | November 2026 \r\n       \r\n     \r\n     \r\n     \r\n     \r\n     \r\n     \r\n     \r\n     \r\n     \r\n     \r\n     \r\n     \r\n     \r\n     \r\n     \r\n     \r\n\t\r\n\t\r\n\t \r\n\t\r\n\t \r\n     \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n        \r\n\t\r\n\t \r\n\t \r\n     \r\n\t\r\n\t    \r\n     \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n      \n \n \n   \r\n\t\r\n \r\n \r\n\t \r\n\t \r\n    \r\n     \r\n\t\r\n\t             We’re currently experiencing an incident. Follow live updates on our status page                   We’re currently experiencing an incident. Follow live updates on our status page                            Product              Solutions              Resources               Pricing              Login          Start for free           Talk to us                             Talk to us                                      Login          Start for free           Talk to us                                       Product              Solutions              Resources               Pricing              Login          Start for free           Talk to us                        status      Security   incident       Tue, Nov 3, 2026, 16:21 CET    The GitBook app, the GitBook API, and published docs are available again. A few services may still be degraded as we finish restoring everything to full performance.   What happened   GitBook has been the target of a sophisticated, highly targeted attack using AI agents.   At 19:00 CET, November 2, the attacker gained unauthorized access to some of our infrastructure credentials. We detected the attack immediately and acted swiftly to block further impact.   To make sure our infrastructure was fully secure, we then took the GitBook app and authenticated docs sites offline. We kept publicly published content live for as long as possible, using cached data.   What we did immediately     Blocked the attacker and closed the vulnerabilities involved    Replaced every credential and secret across our infrastructure    Brought services back only once we were confident they were secure    Invalidated every customer’s API tokens on our platform     Your data   Our investigation shows that the attacker may have accessed the following:    Integrations tokens    Git Sync secrets    API tokens    Questions asked to GitBook Assistant by your site visitors    At this stage, we have found no evidence that any of your content in GitBook was modified.   What you need to do now     Rotate any existing GitBook API tokens. We revoked all personal API tokens during the incident.    Rotate any third-party API tokens or secrets you use to connect other tools to GitBook.    If you have published integrations that use secrets, rotate those secrets.    If you use the GitBook MCP server, re-authenticate it.    Please contact your GitBook organization’s admin to assist with this process.   What we are doing next     Monitoring the situation in case of further attacks.    Introducing further security measures to our platform.    Writing a full post mortem that will be published soon with more detailed information about the incident.    If you have any further questions, please reach out to your account manager or   our support team  . You can also check   status.gitbook.com   for updates  Thank you for your patience, and we apologize again for the disruption   The GitBook Team       Tue, Nov 3, 2026, 13:15 cet    Yesterday, November 2, we detected a security incident affecting GitBook’s infrastructure. We contained it quickly and, as a precaution, we’ve taken some services offline while we secure our systems. We apologize for the disruption this is causing, but your security is our number one priority.  This is a platform wide issue affecting a number of customers. We’re actively working on a fix and will have an update for you in the coming hours.   What happened:  We detected and contained unauthorised access to parts of GitBook’s infrastructure.   Service status:  Some services are temporarily offline as a precaution and will be restored once systems are confirmed secure.   Customer data:  The investigation is ongoing. We will confirm whether any data was affected once the review is complete.   Action required:  None at this time. We’ll share instructions on any steps you may need to take once services are restored.   Updates:  Live updates are available at   status.gitbook.com  . We’ll share a full post-incident report once the investigation is complete.  If you have any questions, please   reach out to our support team   or contact your account manager  Thank you for bearing with us, we apologize again for the inconvenience.   The GitBook Team           FAQs          Is my data compromised?                     Why are some GitBook services offline?                     What are you doing to solve the problem?                     Do I need to do anything right now?                     Where can I get updates or ask questions?                                                              Product           Pricing                                AI Tools             GitBook Agent                                   GitBook Assistant                                   Docs Analytics                                  connectors             GitBook MCP     New                                    Custom components                                   Built-in extensions                                  Create & Publish             Git Sync                                   Authenticated access                                   Editor                                 Solutions       Use case             Public docs                                   API docs                                   Help center                                   Knowledge base                                   Open source                                  industry         